#19804
Atop a Dangerous Cliff~
While a path lies to the north, all that lies south is thin air.  In fact, the
altitude here is so great that thin cloud cover blocks visibility downward,
making it impossible to tell what lies below.  Perhaps it is water, perhaps
sharp rocks; in either case, the path to the north looks like a more inviting
place.
~
198 32768 0 0 0 5
D0
~
~
0 0 19802
D2
~
~
0 0 19805
S
#19805
Falling~
All that surrounds you is air; there is nothing to grab hold of, nothing to
stop your downward descent into the unknown.  Fortunately, you fell off a high
enough altitude to enjoy what might be your last few seconds of life.  There
is still a chance to escape by magical means, or face the abysmal mist below.
~
198 68 0 0 0 9
D0
~
~
0 0 19804
D5
~
~
